{"lines": ["In 1518, a whole city caught a plague, and the only symptom was dancing.", "One July day in Strasbourg, a woman called Frau Troffea stepped outside and started to dance.", "There was no music.", "She just could not stop.", "She danced for nearly a week, and instead of stopping her, the neighbours joined in.", "So the city's doctors studied the problem, and blamed hot blood.", "Their cure?", "More dancing.", "The council opened halls, hired a band, and even paid strong men to hold the dancers up.", "This did not help. By August, up to four hundred people were dancing.", "And this is where the joke stops being funny.", "Their feet swelled and bled into their shoes. They screamed for help, but could not stop.", "Dancers collapsed. Later accounts say some died, though historians still argue how many.", "Finally, the council banned music.", "The dancers were taken to a mountain shrine of Saint Vitus, and by September, it stopped.", "Some blame a mould on rye bread that causes spasms.", "But most historians blame fear, because after years of famine and disease, people believed Saint Vitus cursed sinners with dancing.", "So was it a curse, a mould, or a city so full of fear it danced?"], "words": [["In", 0.0, 0.06], ["1518,", 0.06, 1.42], ["a", 1.98, 2.1], ["whole", 2.1, 2.26], ["city", 2.26, 2.52], ["caught", 2.52, 2.8], ["a", 2.8, 2.94], ["plague,", 2.94, 3.14], ["and", 3.78, 3.84], ["the", 3.84, 3.92], ["only", 3.92, 4.12], ["symptom", 4.12, 4.5], ["was", 4.5, 4.82], ["dancing.", 4.82, 5.04], ["One", 5.958, 6.08], ["July", 6.08, 6.3], ["day", 6.3, 6.7], ["in", 6.7, 6.88], ["Strasbourg,", 6.88, 7.42], ["a", 7.88, 8.02], ["woman", 8.02, 8.22], ["called", 8.22, 8.52], ["Frau", 8.52, 8.92], ["Troffea", 8.92, 9.38], ["stepped", 9.38, 9.62], ["outside", 9.62, 10.14], ["and", 10.14, 10.36], ["started", 10.36, 10.66], ["to", 10.66, 10.82], ["dance.", 10.82, 11.04], ["There", 11.614, 11.7], ["was", 11.7, 11.8], ["no", 11.8, 12.0], ["music.", 12.0, 12.38], ["She", 13.